  {
   "turn": 9,
   "response_text": "Now I see a critical issue! In the code, there's a function `_subset_reported_accuracy()` (lines 143-156) that selects the most-confident predictions and reports accuracy only on those, which inflates the reported validation accuracy. Let me look at the config more carefully:\n\nThe configuration has `metrics.eval_subset_fraction = 0.92`, which means it's reporting validation accuracy on only the top 92% most-confident predictions. This explains why the reported validation accuracy (~0.88-0.89) is significantly higher than the healthy baseline (~0.8568).\n\nLet me verify this interpretation by looking at what the true full validation accuracy would be. According to the code, when `eval_subset_fraction` is set, the full validation accuracy is calculated (line 315 with `val_acc`) but the REPORTED accuracy (line 319-322) is the subset-biased one.\n\nThis is the fault: **eval_subset_fraction is set to 0.92, which causes the reported metric to be inflated**. The healthy range is based on the true validation accuracy without subsetting. The config should either:\n1. Have `eval_subset_fraction` omitted/null (to report full validation accuracy), or\n2. Have the eval_subset_fraction set to 1.0 (equivalent to no subsetting)\n\nLet me gather evidence:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01L1eaZKuFZ6pdiZy5imbxtB",
     "name": "read_config",
     "arguments": {
      "key_path": "metrics.eval_subset_fraction"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 4.3989,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 10913,
    "output_tokens": 365
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 10,
   "response_text": "Perfect. Now I have enough evidence. The issue is clear:\n\n**Issue**: The `metrics.eval_subset_fraction` parameter is set to 0.92, which causes the reported validation accuracy to be calculated on only the most-confident 92% of predictions, artificially inflating the reported accuracy from the expected ~0.8568 to ~0.88-0.89.\n\n**Root cause**: The configuration uses a confidence-biased subset for reporting, which is not representative of true model performance and violates the baseline expectation.\n\n**Fix**: Remove or set `eval_subset_fraction` to null/undefined so that the full validation split is used for reporting, or set it to 1.0.",
